1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,212
Sweetheart, on Christmas Day in our house,

2
00:00:03,212 --> 00:00:05,353
the ham came out of the oven

3
00:00:05,353 --> 00:00:07,418
shining like stained glass.

4
00:00:07,598 --> 00:00:08,848
Dark amber glaze,

5
00:00:08,848 --> 00:00:11,420
a diamond pattern cut into the top,

6
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:13,477
and a clove in the middle of

7
00:00:13,477 --> 00:00:14,506
every diamond.

8
00:00:14,686 --> 00:00:16,829
My father carried it to the table

9
00:00:16,829 --> 00:00:19,426
on my grandmother's blue platter like he

10
00:00:19,426 --> 00:00:21,374
was carrying the crown jewels.

11
00:00:21,554 --> 00:00:23,585
And the whole family clapped.

12
00:00:23,765 --> 00:00:24,961
Every year.

13
00:00:25,312 --> 00:00:28,161
But today, people tell me their Christmas

14
00:00:28,161 --> 00:00:30,245
ham comes out dry and stringy,

15
00:00:30,245 --> 00:00:32,330
or so salty you need a pitcher

16
00:00:32,330 --> 00:00:34,762
of water, or the glaze burns black.

17
00:00:34,942 --> 00:00:37,503
So tonight I'm giving you my brown

18
00:00:37,503 --> 00:00:38,783
sugar glazed ham,

19
00:00:38,783 --> 00:00:41,644
every step, and the five mistakes that

20
00:00:41,644 --> 00:00:43,301
make it dry and salty.

21
00:00:43,481 --> 00:00:44,724
And stay with me,

22
00:00:44,724 --> 00:00:47,137
because the last trick is when to

23
00:00:47,137 --> 00:00:48,380
put on the glaze,

24
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:51,086
and it's the reason most glazes burn.

25
00:00:51,436 --> 00:00:54,354
Ham at Christmas is an old tradition,

26
00:00:54,354 --> 00:00:56,405
honey, older than America.

27
00:00:56,585 --> 00:00:57,768
In the old days,

28
00:00:57,768 --> 00:01:00,505
farm families butchered a hog in late

29
00:01:00,505 --> 00:01:03,167
fall, and salted and smoked the hams

30
00:01:03,167 --> 00:01:05,164
to keep through the winter.

31
00:01:05,344 --> 00:01:08,084
The best ham was saved for Christmas.

32
00:01:08,264 --> 00:01:09,997
On Grandma Pearl's farm,

33
00:01:09,997 --> 00:01:12,596
the hams hung in the smokehouse from

34
00:01:12,596 --> 00:01:14,834
November, and on Christmas Eve,

35
00:01:14,834 --> 00:01:17,650
my grandfather would take one down like

36
00:01:17,650 --> 00:01:19,816
he was picking the best apple.

37
00:01:20,167 --> 00:01:22,054
By the time I was cooking,

38
00:01:22,054 --> 00:01:23,143
in the sixties,

39
00:01:23,143 --> 00:01:26,119
everybody bought their ham at the grocery

40
00:01:26,119 --> 00:01:28,514
store, already cooked and smoked.

41
00:01:28,694 --> 00:01:31,376
That's what most hams are today.

42
00:01:31,556 --> 00:01:34,356
And that changes everything about how you

43
00:01:34,356 --> 00:01:37,224
cook it, because you're not really cooking

44
00:01:37,224 --> 00:01:37,907
it, honey.

45
00:01:38,087 --> 00:01:39,640
You're only warming it,

46
00:01:39,640 --> 00:01:40,652
and glazing it.

47
00:01:40,832 --> 00:01:42,869
In a minute I'll tell you why

48
00:01:42,869 --> 00:01:45,186
that's the secret to a juicy ham.

49
00:01:45,537 --> 00:01:48,141
And my mother's Christmas ham was the

50
00:01:48,141 --> 00:01:50,746
one dinner she never let anybody help

51
00:01:50,746 --> 00:01:51,098
with.

52
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:53,268
She'd shoo us all out of the

53
00:01:53,268 --> 00:01:55,328
kitchen on Christmas morning,

54
00:01:55,328 --> 00:01:57,744
while we played with our presents.

55
00:01:57,924 --> 00:02:00,067
Danny and I would sneak to the

56
00:02:00,067 --> 00:02:02,709
kitchen door and smell it through the

57
00:02:02,709 --> 00:02:03,137
crack.

58
00:02:03,317 --> 00:02:05,307
Brown sugar, cloves,

59
00:02:05,307 --> 00:02:06,301
and smoke.

60
00:02:06,481 --> 00:02:07,445
To this day,

61
00:02:07,445 --> 00:02:10,418
that smell means Christmas to me more

62
00:02:10,418 --> 00:02:12,588
than any tree or any carol.

63
00:02:12,938 --> 00:02:15,422
First, choosing the ham.

64
00:02:15,602 --> 00:02:17,581
Look for a fully cooked,

65
00:02:17,581 --> 00:02:20,384
bone-in ham, either a shank end or

66
00:02:20,384 --> 00:02:21,291
a butt end,

67
00:02:21,291 --> 00:02:22,940
eight to ten pounds.

68
00:02:23,120 --> 00:02:26,278
That feeds twelve people with leftovers.

69
00:02:26,458 --> 00:02:29,138
Bone-in is juicier and has more flavor

70
00:02:29,138 --> 00:02:31,607
than boneless, and you get the bone

71
00:02:31,607 --> 00:02:32,947
for soup afterward.

72
00:02:33,127 --> 00:02:34,768
My mother always said,

73
00:02:34,768 --> 00:02:36,855
the bone is the best part of

74
00:02:36,855 --> 00:02:38,943
the ham, and the soup is the

75
00:02:38,943 --> 00:02:40,732
best part of New Year's.

76
00:02:41,082 --> 00:02:43,531
And here's mistake number one.

77
00:02:43,711 --> 00:02:45,964
Buying a ham with water added.

78
00:02:46,144 --> 00:02:47,423
Read the label,

79
00:02:47,423 --> 00:02:48,361
sweetheart.

80
00:02:48,541 --> 00:02:51,360
If it says ham with natural juices,

81
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:52,326
that's good.

82
00:02:52,506 --> 00:02:53,808
If it says ham,

83
00:02:53,808 --> 00:02:57,107
water added, or ham and water product,

84
00:02:57,107 --> 00:03:00,319
it's been pumped full of salty water.

85
00:03:00,499 --> 00:03:02,357
It shrinks in the oven,

86
00:03:02,357 --> 00:03:03,729
tastes like salt,

87
00:03:03,729 --> 00:03:05,828
and the texture is spongy.

88
00:03:06,008 --> 00:03:08,473
Pay the extra dollar for a better

89
00:03:08,473 --> 00:03:08,772
ham.

90
00:03:09,122 --> 00:03:11,414
And spiral-cut hams are easy,

91
00:03:11,414 --> 00:03:13,707
but they dry out the fastest,

92
00:03:13,707 --> 00:03:16,712
because all those slices let the juice

93
00:03:16,712 --> 00:03:17,028
out.

94
00:03:17,208 --> 00:03:18,585
If you buy one,

95
00:03:18,585 --> 00:03:20,238
cook it face down,

96
00:03:20,238 --> 00:03:22,258
wrapped tight in foil,

97
00:03:22,258 --> 00:03:24,186
and watch it closely.

98
00:03:24,366 --> 00:03:26,252
I like a whole ham that I

99
00:03:26,252 --> 00:03:27,233
score myself.

100
00:03:27,413 --> 00:03:28,696
It stays juicier,

101
00:03:28,696 --> 00:03:31,337
and it looks prettier on the table.

102
00:03:31,517 --> 00:03:33,561
That's how my father liked it.

103
00:03:33,911 --> 00:03:35,048
Step one.

104
00:03:35,228 --> 00:03:37,398
Take the ham out of the icebox

105
00:03:37,398 --> 00:03:39,641
two hours before it goes in the

106
00:03:39,641 --> 00:03:41,811
oven, so it warms up a little.

107
00:03:41,991 --> 00:03:45,056
Mistake number two is putting an ice-cold

108
00:03:45,056 --> 00:03:46,252
ham in the oven.

109
00:03:46,432 --> 00:03:48,987
The outside dries out while you wait

110
00:03:48,987 --> 00:03:50,832
for the middle to warm up.

111
00:03:51,012 --> 00:03:53,822
Heat the oven to three hundred twenty-five.

112
00:03:54,002 --> 00:03:55,012
Not hotter.

113
00:03:55,362 --> 00:03:57,196
Step two, scoring.

114
00:03:57,376 --> 00:03:58,812
With a sharp knife,

115
00:03:58,812 --> 00:04:01,382
cut a diamond pattern into the fat

116
00:04:01,382 --> 00:04:03,574
on top, about a quarter of an

117
00:04:03,574 --> 00:04:04,330
inch deep.

118
00:04:04,510 --> 00:04:06,773
Cut lines one inch apart in one

119
00:04:06,773 --> 00:04:09,254
direction, and then the other way,

120
00:04:09,254 --> 00:04:10,130
across them.

121
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:12,446
Don't cut too deep into the meat.

122
00:04:12,626 --> 00:04:14,699
Then press a whole clove into the

123
00:04:14,699 --> 00:04:16,144
middle of each diamond.

124
00:04:16,324 --> 00:04:18,566
The cuts let the glaze sink in,

125
00:04:18,566 --> 00:04:20,953
and the cloves make it smell like

126
00:04:20,953 --> 00:04:21,676
Christmas.

127
00:04:22,026 --> 00:04:23,175
Step three.

128
00:04:23,355 --> 00:04:24,507
Put the ham,

129
00:04:24,507 --> 00:04:25,852
cut side down,

130
00:04:25,852 --> 00:04:27,581
in a roasting pan.

131
00:04:27,761 --> 00:04:29,707
Pour about a cup of water or

132
00:04:29,707 --> 00:04:32,069
apple juice into the bottom of the

133
00:04:32,069 --> 00:04:32,347
pan.

134
00:04:32,527 --> 00:04:35,104
Then cover the whole pan tightly with

135
00:04:35,104 --> 00:04:35,453
foil.

136
00:04:35,633 --> 00:04:38,924
Mistake number three is roasting it uncovered

137
00:04:38,924 --> 00:04:40,021
at a high heat.

138
00:04:40,201 --> 00:04:42,361
The foil keeps the steam in,

139
00:04:42,361 --> 00:04:44,907
and the steam keeps the ham juicy

140
00:04:44,907 --> 00:04:46,064
while it warms.

141
00:04:46,415 --> 00:04:48,167
If this is helping you,

142
00:04:48,167 --> 00:04:50,757
honey, tap the like button for me.

143
00:04:50,937 --> 00:04:53,630
It helps Grandma more than you know.

144
00:04:53,810 --> 00:04:56,627
Now, bake it at three twenty-five for

145
00:04:56,627 --> 00:04:59,824
about twelve to fifteen minutes per pound.

146
00:05:00,004 --> 00:05:02,360
An eight pound ham takes about an

147
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:05,287
hour and forty-five minutes to two hours.

148
00:05:05,467 --> 00:05:07,350
But use a thermometer,

149
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:08,892
like I always say.

150
00:05:09,072 --> 00:05:11,315
A fully cooked ham only needs to

151
00:05:11,315 --> 00:05:13,979
reach one hundred forty degrees in the

152
00:05:13,979 --> 00:05:14,470
middle.

153
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:17,218
And here's mistake number four,

154
00:05:17,218 --> 00:05:19,461
the one that makes it dry and

155
00:05:19,461 --> 00:05:20,080
stringy.

156
00:05:20,260 --> 00:05:21,845
Cooking it too long,

157
00:05:21,845 --> 00:05:24,697
until it's one sixty or one seventy,

158
00:05:24,697 --> 00:05:26,599
like a fresh pork roast.

159
00:05:26,779 --> 00:05:29,159
Remember, it's already cooked.

160
00:05:29,339 --> 00:05:30,779
You're only warming it.

161
00:05:30,959 --> 00:05:32,947
Once it's past one forty,

162
00:05:32,947 --> 00:05:35,889
every minute in the oven squeezes out

163
00:05:35,889 --> 00:05:36,764
more juice.

164
00:05:36,944 --> 00:05:38,813
Take it out at one thirty,

165
00:05:38,813 --> 00:05:41,113
glaze it, and it'll be one forty

166
00:05:41,113 --> 00:05:42,191
when it's done.

167
00:05:42,541 --> 00:05:43,877
Now the glaze.

168
00:05:44,057 --> 00:05:45,639
While the ham warms,

169
00:05:45,639 --> 00:05:47,853
make it in a small saucepan.

170
00:05:48,033 --> 00:05:50,715
One cup of packed brown sugar.

171
00:05:50,895 --> 00:05:52,706
A quarter cup of honey.

172
00:05:52,886 --> 00:05:56,345
Two tablespoons of Dijon or spicy brown

173
00:05:56,345 --> 00:05:57,054
mustard.

174
00:05:57,234 --> 00:06:00,912
Two tablespoons of orange juice or pineapple

175
00:06:00,912 --> 00:06:01,414
juice.

176
00:06:01,594 --> 00:06:04,589
A pinch of ground cloves and cinnamon.

177
00:06:04,769 --> 00:06:06,849
Stir it over low heat for three

178
00:06:06,849 --> 00:06:09,332
or four minutes until it's smooth and

179
00:06:09,332 --> 00:06:09,936
bubbling.

180
00:06:10,285 --> 00:06:12,361
The mustard is the secret,

181
00:06:12,361 --> 00:06:12,840
honey.

182
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:15,517
It cuts through the sweetness and the

183
00:06:15,517 --> 00:06:18,013
salt, so the glaze doesn't taste like

184
00:06:18,013 --> 00:06:18,418
candy.

185
00:06:18,598 --> 00:06:20,751
My mother used a spoon of her

186
00:06:20,751 --> 00:06:23,201
own pickle juice from the cellar,

187
00:06:23,201 --> 00:06:23,498
too.

188
00:06:23,678 --> 00:06:25,584
And for a Christmas twist,

189
00:06:25,584 --> 00:06:27,857
add two tablespoons of bourbon.

190
00:06:28,037 --> 00:06:30,319
My husband said that ham was the

191
00:06:30,319 --> 00:06:32,743
only reason he went to church that

192
00:06:32,743 --> 00:06:33,099
year.

193
00:06:33,449 --> 00:06:36,415
So far, a bone-in ham with natural

194
00:06:36,415 --> 00:06:39,206
juices, out of the icebox early,

195
00:06:39,206 --> 00:06:41,910
scored and studded with cloves,

196
00:06:41,910 --> 00:06:44,004
covered tight with foil,

197
00:06:44,004 --> 00:06:45,137
low and slow,

198
00:06:45,137 --> 00:06:47,056
and only to one forty.

199
00:06:47,236 --> 00:06:48,978
Now the trick I promised,

200
00:06:48,978 --> 00:06:51,137
about when to put on the glaze.

201
00:06:51,317 --> 00:06:54,042
Mistake number five is glazing the ham

202
00:06:54,042 --> 00:06:54,974
at the start.

203
00:06:55,154 --> 00:06:57,453
Sugar can't take two hours in the

204
00:06:57,453 --> 00:06:57,802
oven.

205
00:06:57,982 --> 00:07:00,014
It burns black and bitter,

206
00:07:00,014 --> 00:07:02,359
and it smokes up your kitchen.

207
00:07:02,708 --> 00:07:03,928
Here's how.

208
00:07:04,108 --> 00:07:06,834
When the ham reaches one hundred thirty

209
00:07:06,834 --> 00:07:09,140
degrees, take it out and turn the

210
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:10,818
oven up to four hundred.

211
00:07:10,998 --> 00:07:12,484
Take off the foil.

212
00:07:12,664 --> 00:07:15,364
Brush half the glaze all over the

213
00:07:15,364 --> 00:07:16,509
top and sides,

214
00:07:16,509 --> 00:07:17,982
into all the cuts.

215
00:07:18,162 --> 00:07:19,530
Put it back in,

216
00:07:19,530 --> 00:07:21,993
uncovered, for ten minutes.

217
00:07:22,173 --> 00:07:24,378
Then brush on the rest of the

218
00:07:24,378 --> 00:07:27,116
glaze, and give it ten more minutes,

219
00:07:27,116 --> 00:07:30,006
until it's bubbling and shiny and dark

220
00:07:30,006 --> 00:07:30,462
amber.

221
00:07:30,812 --> 00:07:33,809
Watch it closely those last minutes,

222
00:07:33,809 --> 00:07:34,725
sweetheart.

223
00:07:34,905 --> 00:07:37,972
Sugar goes from beautiful to burnt very

224
00:07:37,972 --> 00:07:38,365
fast.

225
00:07:38,545 --> 00:07:40,434
If the edges get too dark,

226
00:07:40,434 --> 00:07:42,469
lay a little foil over them.

227
00:07:42,649 --> 00:07:45,362
And spoon the drippings from the pan

228
00:07:45,362 --> 00:07:47,397
over the ham once or twice.

229
00:07:47,577 --> 00:07:50,258
That's what gives it that stained glass

230
00:07:50,258 --> 00:07:52,802
shine my father carried to the table.

231
00:07:53,151 --> 00:07:55,380
And here's an old trick for a

232
00:07:55,380 --> 00:07:56,840
fancier ham, honey,

233
00:07:56,840 --> 00:07:59,761
the one from the magazines in nineteen

234
00:07:59,761 --> 00:08:00,222
sixty.

235
00:08:00,402 --> 00:08:02,893
Pin pineapple rings all over the ham

236
00:08:02,893 --> 00:08:05,522
with toothpicks before the last glaze,

237
00:08:05,522 --> 00:08:08,152
with a maraschino cherry in the middle

238
00:08:08,152 --> 00:08:09,051
of each ring.

239
00:08:09,231 --> 00:08:11,008
It looks like a party.

240
00:08:11,188 --> 00:08:14,708
My granddaughter thinks it's the silliest thing

241
00:08:14,708 --> 00:08:15,681
she ever saw,

242
00:08:15,681 --> 00:08:18,003
and she asks for it every year.

243
00:08:18,352 --> 00:08:20,578
Let it rest twenty minutes,

244
00:08:20,578 --> 00:08:22,721
covered loosely with foil,

245
00:08:22,721 --> 00:08:24,122
before you carve,

246
00:08:24,122 --> 00:08:25,853
so the juices settle.

247
00:08:26,033 --> 00:08:28,673
To carve, cut along the bone to

248
00:08:28,673 --> 00:08:30,377
take off big pieces,

249
00:08:30,377 --> 00:08:33,699
then slice each piece across the grain,

250
00:08:33,699 --> 00:08:34,125
thin.

251
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:36,925
Put the slices on a warm platter,

252
00:08:36,925 --> 00:08:39,466
and spoon the pan juices and any

253
00:08:39,466 --> 00:08:41,213
extra glaze over them.

254
00:08:41,393 --> 00:08:44,036
Nobody ever needs a glass of water

255
00:08:44,036 --> 00:08:44,968
at my table.

256
00:08:45,318 --> 00:08:48,221
And serve it the old Ohio way,

257
00:08:48,221 --> 00:08:48,801
honey.

258
00:08:48,981 --> 00:08:51,805
Scalloped potatoes, green beans,

259
00:08:51,805 --> 00:08:54,981
a jar of my mother's spiced peaches,

260
00:08:54,981 --> 00:08:57,364
and warm rolls with butter.

261
00:08:57,544 --> 00:08:59,796
And a little bowl of spicy brown

262
00:08:59,796 --> 00:09:02,049
mustard on the side for the men.

263
00:09:02,229 --> 00:09:04,910
My father put mustard on everything.

264
00:09:05,090 --> 00:09:06,910
My mother said he'd put it on

265
00:09:06,910 --> 00:09:08,980
the Christmas pie if she let him.

266
00:09:09,329 --> 00:09:12,421
Leftover ham keeps five days in the

267
00:09:12,421 --> 00:09:15,512
icebox, and freezes for two months,

268
00:09:15,512 --> 00:09:16,748
wrapped tight.

269
00:09:16,928 --> 00:09:19,552
Ham sandwiches on Boxing Day.

270
00:09:19,732 --> 00:09:21,996
Ham and eggs on Sunday.

271
00:09:22,176 --> 00:09:24,452
Ham and cheese in a casserole.

272
00:09:24,632 --> 00:09:26,558
And save that bone,

273
00:09:26,558 --> 00:09:27,673
sweetheart.

274
00:09:27,853 --> 00:09:29,641
Put it in a big pot with

275
00:09:29,641 --> 00:09:31,875
a pound of dried split peas or

276
00:09:31,875 --> 00:09:34,408
navy beans, an onion and a carrot,

277
00:09:34,408 --> 00:09:36,642
and simmer it for three hours.

278
00:09:36,822 --> 00:09:39,040
That's the best soup of the whole

279
00:09:39,040 --> 00:09:39,376
year.

280
00:09:39,726 --> 00:09:41,085
So one more time.

281
00:09:41,265 --> 00:09:44,130
Bone-in ham, with natural juices,

282
00:09:44,130 --> 00:09:45,433
no water added.

283
00:09:45,613 --> 00:09:48,434
Out of the icebox two hours early.

284
00:09:48,614 --> 00:09:50,100
Score it, clove it.

285
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,633
Cut side down,

286
00:09:51,633 --> 00:09:53,083
a cup of juice,

287
00:09:53,083 --> 00:09:54,437
covered tight.

288
00:09:54,617 --> 00:09:57,589
Three twenty-five, only to one thirty.

289
00:09:57,769 --> 00:09:58,942
Then the glaze,

290
00:09:58,942 --> 00:09:59,958
in two coats,

291
00:09:59,958 --> 00:10:01,835
the last twenty minutes,

292
00:10:01,835 --> 00:10:03,086
at four hundred.

293
00:10:03,266 --> 00:10:05,901
Rest it, and slice it thin.

294
00:10:06,081 --> 00:10:09,062
That's a Christmas ham that's never dry

295
00:10:09,062 --> 00:10:10,284
and never salty.

296
00:10:10,634 --> 00:10:12,314
Tell me in the comments,

297
00:10:12,314 --> 00:10:13,084
sweetheart.

298
00:10:13,264 --> 00:10:15,868
Ham or turkey for Christmas dinner at

299
00:10:15,868 --> 00:10:16,643
your house?

300
00:10:16,823 --> 00:10:19,203
Or both, like mine?

301
00:10:19,383 --> 00:10:22,503
The whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

302
00:10:22,503 --> 00:10:24,508
right there on your screen,

303
00:10:24,508 --> 00:10:26,588
and I'll see you in the next

304
00:10:26,588 --> 00:10:27,034
video.

305
00:10:27,214 --> 00:10:29,002
Good night, honey.

306
00:10:29,182 --> 00:10:30,459
Merry Christmas.
